      "excluded": "The coherence of the outer six-family and the cross-golden determinant comparison are checked.  Renaming the six labels along the inverse of each of the six reorderings carries the fixed conference matrix to a symmetric matrix with vanishing diagonal, unit off-diagonal squares and square 5 * 1, whose triangle products are the coefficients of the corresponding translate; the six resulting sign words are pairwise distinct and each obeys the four-point two-graph identity.  Over a commutative ring with two invertible and an invertible square root s of five, the two golden projectors are symmetric, sum to the identity and are idempotent, the commutator of the diagonal matrix of the coordinates with the conference matrix is 2 s times the antisymmetric part of the cross-golden block, and the triangle cubic satisfies Z^2 = 500 det (B - B^T) = (10 s Pf (B - B^T))^2, hence over an integral domain Z = +- 10 s Pf (B - B^T).  The determinant-square identity is checked: the determinant of an order-six skew-symmetric matrix with vanishing diagonal is the square of its Pfaffian, so the determinant of the fixed conference bracket matrix is sixteen times the square of its triangle cubic.  Not formalized: the comparison of that Pfaffian with the determinant of a three-by-three matrix representing the induced map between the two spectral spaces in a chosen pair of orthonormal frames, which is a choice of bases the statements above avoid."
